{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QSS2EQ5ftrhUwYUbxwbayR","type":"tool_result","content":"# offline replica, data as of 2026-03-01T00:00:00Z\nid:\t74954004f83dfbbd96fb4d41\nlist:\tdev@kafka.apache.org\nfrom:\tFederico Valeri\ndate:\t2026-02-14T07:17:27Z\nsubject:\t[DISCUSS] KIP-1279: Cluster Mirroring\nthread:\tCAMeNjWJ28d1670e424eKLFym79z826O1AT-pBztGg8OJakPqnw@mail.gmail.com\n\nHi, we would like to start a discussion thread about KIP-1279: Cluster\nMirroring.\n\nCluster Mirroring is a new Kafka feature that enables native,\nbroker-level topic replication across clusters. Unlike MirrorMaker 2\n(which runs as an external Connect-based tool), Cluster Mirroring is\nbuilt into the broker itself, allowing tighter integration with the\ncontroller, coordinator, and partition lifecycle.\n\nhttps://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/KAFKA/KIP-1279%3A+Cluster+Mirroring\n\nThere are a few missing bits, but most of the design is there, so we\nthink it is the right time to involve the community and get feedback.\nPlease help validating our approach.\n\nThanks\nFede","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e26104f8-1506-48bf-952d-9763f72b7b28","uuid":"9f4e3b3c-8e71-4cf8-90ce-b7c8e1d99493","timestamp":"2026-09-27T19:54:00.960Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# offline replica, data as of 2026-03-01T00:00:00Z\nid:\t74954004f83dfbbd96fb4d41\nlist:\tdev@kafka.apache.org\nfrom:\tFederico Valeri\ndate:\t2026-02-14T07:17:27Z\nsubject:\t[DISCUSS] KIP-1279: Cluster Mirroring\nthread:\tCAMeNjWJ28d1670e424eKLFym79z826O1AT-pBztGg8OJakPqnw@mail.gmail.com\n\nHi, we would like to start a discussion thread about KIP-1279: Cluster\nMirroring.\n\nCluster Mirroring is a new Kafka feature that enables native,\nbroker-level topic replication across clusters. Unlike MirrorMaker 2\n(which runs as an external Connect-based tool), Cluster Mirroring is\nbuilt into the broker itself, allowing tighter integration with the\ncontroller, coordinator, and partition lifecycle.\n\nhttps://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/KAFKA/KIP-1279%3A+Cluster+Mirroring\n\nThere are a few missing bits, but most of the design is there, so we\nthink it is the right time to involve the community and get feedback.\nPlease help validating our approach.\n\nThanks\nFede","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
